🔹 Algorithm (2 Pointer Approach)
Initialize two pointers:
i = 0 (firstList)
j = 0 (secondList)
While both lists are not exhausted:
Take intervals:
[s1, e1] from firstList
[s2, e2] from secondList
Find intersection:
start = max(s1, s2)
end = min(e1, e2)
If start <= end:
Add [start, end] to result
Move the pointer of the interval which ends first:
If e1 < e2 → i++
Else → j++
Time Complexity
Each interval is processed once
👉 O(n + m)
🔹 Space Complexity
Only result list used
👉 O(1) (excluding output)
